"Current analyses often involve large datasets of 400-500 samples. For visualizing these, phylogenetic trees created with tools like the handy and free iTOL are common. 
However, manually coloring each node in iTOL can be tedious. To simplify this, I'm sharing a metadata file template below that demonstrates the required format. 
This will allow you to create these files easily. It took me some time to figure this out, so I'm sharing it freely to help the scientific community. 
I recommend using a text editor like Notepad++ to create or modify this file."


